course: dictionary
lesson: 13241
title: Real or fake, honest or not
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Genuineness is a noun. It names the quality of being genuine. Genuine means real and not fake, and it can also mean honest and sincere. Genuineness is uncountable, so you say "the genuineness of", not "a genuineness".
explain: «The expert tested the genuineness of the old coin.» Here genuineness means the coin is real, not a copy. The expert wanted to know if it was true gold and history, or a fake.
explain: «Mia could see the genuineness of his smile, so she believed him.» Here genuineness means he really meant it. His smile was honest, not an act.
fact: Genuineness is a noun, and it names how genuine something or someone is.
fact: Genuineness has two meanings: being real and not fake, and being honest and sincere.
fact: «Genuine» means real, not fake. «Sincere» means really meaning what you say or feel.
fact: «Doubt the genuineness of» means you are not sure something is real.
fact: «Test its genuineness» means check whether something is real or fake.
exercise: «The shop checked the genuineness of the gold ring.» What does genuineness mean here? | Being cheap and old | Being very heavy | *Being real, not fake | Being very shiny
exercise: «Her friends never doubted the genuineness of her kindness.» What does genuineness mean here? | Being loud and cheerful | Being a secret | *Being honest and really meaning it | Being late for school
exercise: «The detective wanted to test the genuineness of the old will.» What does test its genuineness mean? | To hide it in a box | To read it aloud | *To check whether it is real | To copy it quickly
test: «The expert doubted the genuineness of the old map.» What does doubted the genuineness mean? | Painted a new map | Was sure the map was new | Lost the map in the park | *Was not sure the map was real
test: «Lily's sorry hug showed the genuineness of her feelings.» What does genuineness show here? | That she was late | That she was tired | That she had a new coat | *That she really meant it
exam: Which is a good way to test the genuineness of a coin? | Eat it to see if it tastes nice | Throw it in the bin | *Compare it with a known real coin and check its metal and marks | Give it to a friend without looking
